  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "JX4W54jYnwDAiwbJZ0aTbeLx5Z0=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:44.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "A **Reactor** is the Powerhouse library (`@powerhousedao/reactor`) that applies reducers, orders operations into a deterministic log, and routes them to processors and sync channels. It is *not* a service: it has no `main()` and it does not open a port. A **host application** embeds it and supplies storage, network, UI surfaces, and the package registry. When you run `ph vetra --watch`, a local host application starts and embeds a Reactor for you. Reactors provide:\n\n- Document storage and hosting\n- Document synchronization across clients\n- Conflict resolution\n- Operation history verification (by rerunning operations)\n\nReactors can be configured for:\n- Local storage (development/Studio Mode)\n- Centralized cloud storage\n- Decentralized storage networks\n\nThe Reactor has no public API of its own \u2014 that surface belongs to the host. **Switchboard**, the API host that wraps a Reactor, is what exposes the GraphQL subgraphs: system, analytics, and per-model subgraphs such as document-editor, vetra-package, subgraph-module, processor-module and app-module, plus vetra-read-model. Switchboard also provides the WebSocket server for subscriptions and the MCP server for AI agent integration.\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:44.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:44.000Z"
    }
  },
